[h2]Polaris interface update[/h2]
Industrial Control has clearer native buttons and selected tabs, with wrapped navigation and actions at narrow widths. Processing, storage and resource accounting are unchanged.
Browser checks do not establish Unity interaction approval. The recent refresh pacing remains in place; further performance recordings are deferred.

[h2]Polaris readability correction[/h2]
Dark button faces now keep labels readable in every interaction state. This fixes the white-button regression reported in game. The corrected native appearance still awaits owner playtesting.

[b]Item handling correction[/b]
Correct loose machinery and conduit pickup/drop actions. D4-S, R4-S and F6-S assembly sections now use the native cumbersome/drag family instead of hand-held scrap behaviour. Sections retain dismantling and remain construction inputs, not installed machines. Existing sections in hands or containers remain where saved. Put a held section down once; future handling uses the drag slot. Requires Phobos Framework 0.30.2. Live menu and inventory handling remain owner-tested.

[b]Merchant and salvage update[/b]
Raise equipment and section offers to at least 85%, and pipes/coolant to at least 95%, before the availability setting. Fill missing functional stock at general local suppliers. Native engineering rolls can now find one of nine intact/damaged machinery families (40% total), one assembly section (15% total), and one pipe/coolant charge (20% total), as separate bounded choices. Normal restocking and new loot generation are required; existing inventories stay as they are. Offline checks are not gameplay validation.

[b]Item-action audit[/b]
The complete item-action audit identified an unresolved inventory-access fault in all F6-P thermal port and F6-R radiator forms. Cargo can remain inside without an Inventory button, hiding Uninstall/Dismantle even when cold. Existing saves must retain that cargo; no recovery fix is included in the audit. Loose conduit stacks require an individual piece for dismantling. D4-S remains a cumbersome construction section, not a finished machine.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/development/item-handling-audit.md]Complete findings and item ledger[/url]

[h2]Assembly and maintenance update[/h2]
D4/R4/F6 final assembly now uses native construction sites, with sections hauled separately. Choose Assembly information on a section. Complete loose machines retain Install. Recover stored cargo provides local access to old F6-P/F6-R contents while blocking new deposits. Maintenance information explains the current blocker.
Offline checks are not Unity gameplay approval. See [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/section-assembly-and-maintenance.md]assembly and maintenance instructions[/url].

[h2]Finding current instructions[/h2]
Use the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/README.md]operating-guide index[/url] for current controls and requirements. Dated research and design records retain their original scope; they are not installation instructions.

[b]Construction appearance work[/b]
D4/R4/F6 construction sites now show unfinished frames while parts arrive, then open machinery once the full bill is delivered and work begins. The finished form appears only after construction completes. Stages follow saved parts and work on reload; removing required parts returns the early appearance. Requires Framework 0.32.0. Offline checks pass; owner visual approval remains pending.
